    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0473" n="461" xml:id="pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/1883: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Earle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-25T13:00:00+02:00">March 25, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Asked Foreign Minister<anchor n="94" xml:id="d476-f1"/> during long
                    discussion if he believed that Russia would overrun Bessarabia in order to
                    retrieve military prestige seriously damaged in Finland. Foreign Minister
                    answered definitely no, giving following reasons. First, Bessarabia has no
                    important strategic objectives such as Finnish positions; Russia already has
                    more than enough undeveloped land and plenty of coast on Black Sea. Second,
                    Germany would oppose such invasion as war would interrupt vital flow of oil to
                    Germany. Third, Stalin wants no war as his position in peace much more secure
                    than in war surrounded by powerful generals. Foreign Minister thinks sturdy
                    Finnish resistance was great surprise to Russian general staff who expected
                    slight resistance not amounting to war.</p>
                <p>Personally believe Foreign Minister neglected to mention importance of
                    controlling the mouth of the Danube.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d476-f1" n="94" xml:id="d476-f1-content">
                <p>Ivan Popov, since February 19, 1940, in Cabinet of Bogdan Filov.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
